#{[17592186516852 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186516760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516852 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516852 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516852 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/64/6486d3914bb0f7b4898220512e96630d13d2b0f4a5c1851938f98371a4c0255f.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n=100$ from a normal population with standard deviation $\\sigma =28.5.$ Given that the mean of the sample is $\\overset{―}{x}=47,$ find a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005,$ where $Z∼N(0,1),$ as shown in the diagram above.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516852 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9fff25a-e37f-5e5a-b519-7f37027d0ee6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516852 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that the population is normally distributed. Therefore, the distribution of sample mean is also normal, and we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\overset{―}{X}-\\mu }{\\sigma /\\sqrt{n}}∼N(0,1),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- $\\mu $ is the population mean,\n\n- ${\\sigma }^{2}$ is the population variance, and\n\n- $n$ is the sample size.\n\nGiven a value $\\alpha $ between $0$ and $1,$ the corresponding $[100(1-\\alpha )]%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the original distribution is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}\\pm {z}_{\\alpha /2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nWe are interested in finding a $99%$ confidence interval. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.99=0.01\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.005.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>2.576)=0.005.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.005}=2.576.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a $99%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ is the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 47\\pm 2.576\\cdot \\frac{28.5}{\\sqrt{100}} \\\\  & 47\\pm 7.342\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516892 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "392ada00-a42a-584f-b062-7d50ce268ef5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516892 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516913 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516913 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66608c24-9189-5e00-8af5-0a05fae7c251" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516913 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516917 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516917 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6b7afb83-fdea-5828-b5b7-adc223e6f2cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516917 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186516852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516938 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516938 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96f61902-b7ed-5f42-b90c-6aa731d477ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516938 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186498533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516968 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186516917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516968 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ced51ab5-0865-5f9e-9ee3-7745ace6a931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186516968 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186515537 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
